from ./Config import Config
from ./Errors import Errors
from ./Formatting import Formatting
from ./Init import Init
from ./OutputSize import OutputSize
from ./Preview import Preview

export anchor Cli:
    description:
        The `emul` command creates, compiles, checks and formats Emul
        projects. It reads `emul.config.pi` from the current directory, if
        there is one, and its flags override the config's settings.

    commands:
        - init
            Creates a new project with a starter config and entry file, as
            described in @{Init}.
        - build
            Checks the project, then renders every composition exported from
            the entry file, in every configured format.
        - check
            Reports errors and warnings without rendering anything.
        - format
            Rewrites `.emul` files in their canonical layout, as described in
            @{Formatting}. With `--check`, it changes nothing and exits with
            code 1 if any file is not already formatted.
        - preview
            Opens a desktop viewer that shows the compositions as SVG or PNG,
            and in the browser as HTML, refreshing by itself whenever a file
            is saved, as described in
            @{Preview}.

    build:
        `emul build` takes optional composition names, to render only those
        compositions instead of all of them.

        ```text
        \\\
        emul build
        emul build Landing SocialCard
        emul build --width 375 --format png --scale 3
        \\\
        ```

    flags:
        - width
            `--width <px>` sets the canvas width.
        - height
            `--height <px>` or `--height auto` sets the canvas height.
        - scale
            `--scale <number>` sets the PNG pixel density.
        - background
            `--background <color>` sets the canvas background, in any colour
            format Emul accepts.
        - format
            `--format <format>` renders only the given format. It may be
            repeated, as in `--format svg --format png`.
        - svgFonts
            `--svg-fonts outline` or `--svg-fonts embed` sets how text is
            written into SVG.
        - outDir
            `--out <dir>` sets the output directory.
        - config
            `--config <path>` uses a config file other than the one in the
            current directory.

    flagPrecedence:
        A size flag applies to every composition being rendered, including
        those with their own sizes in the config, as described in
        @{OutputSize}. Any other flag replaces the matching setting in
        @{Config}.

    exitCodes:
        - 0
            Success. Warnings may have been reported.
        - 1
            One or more errors, as described in @{Errors}. Nothing was
            rendered.
        - 2
            The command itself was used wrongly, such as an unknown flag or a
            composition name that is not exported from the entry, which is
            reported with the code `unknown-composition`.
